// expect: 21
// A PARAMETER DEFAULT READS THE CALLER'S VARIABLE. `b = a + 1` names the
// callee's own `a`, so `f(10)` is 10 + 11. The program answers 243: the
// default's node is spliced into the caller's argument list and lowered in
// the caller's frame, where `a` is main's local 1000, and the sum wraps at
// the exit byte (measured 2026-09-25; `mentl check` is clean). Without the
// caller's `a` the same program traps instead.
//
// SYNTAX §«Default parameter values» says the default is evaluated in the
// callee's parameter scope. Retires when every reference carries its binder
// and lowering reads that edge, so the default's `a` can only be the
// callee's parameter (Hβ.resolve.reference-is-an-edge).
fn f(a, b = a + 1) = a + b

fn main() = {
  let a = 1000
  f(10)
}
